ktree-ops.md","content":"---\nname: train-worktree-ops\ndescription: \"Operational facts for parallel-dispatch train worktrees (C:\\\\Projects\\\\ai-template-trains\\\\*) — which Python/venv to use and how a worker must handle generated artifacts vs the \\\"NEVER edit\\\" contract line.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: c33a8229-9173-4168-8d0e-2fadb9f09bc3\n---\n\nWorking a parallel-dispatch WI in a train worktree under\n`C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\<train>\\` (branch `llm/train/...`):\n\n- **Toolchain venv:** these worktrees have **no local `.venv`**; ambient\n  `python` is old (3.8). Use the **main repo's** venv:\n  `C:\\Projects\\ai-template\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe` (Python **3.11.9**, has\n  pytest/xdist/ruff/pytest-cov). The pre-commit hook's own PY-probe finds no\n  worktree `.venv` and falls back to a PATH 3.12 that lacks ruff, so its\n  `format` step SKIPs — run `ruff format --check`/`check` yourself on the venv.\n\n- **Generated artifacts vs \"NEVER edit\":** the worker prompt says never edit\n  generated artifacts (dashboards, maps). That means don't *hand-edit/reconcile*\n  them — but the universal `.githooks/pre-commit` floor (`check.py --run-steps\n  arch-map,okf,trajectory-map,status-map,...`) **blocks a commit that leaves them\n  stale**. So when your source change stales one, **regenerate via the canonical\n  tool and commit it** (`gen_arch_map.py` for `docs/architecture.md`'s GENERATED\n  block; `gen_trajectory.py --root .` for `PROJECT_STATE.html`; regen order\n  arch-map→okf→dashboard). Precedent: worker commits `WI-219`/`WI-228` bundled a\n  regenerated dashboard. The integrator re-regenerates on the composed tree\n  (stack.ini `[generated]` auto-resolution, WI-235) — no re-review.\n\n- **Still off-limits on a train branch:** `docs/status.md`, `docs/run-state`,\n  `docs/log.md`, and the Status/Deliverable **cells** of `work-items.csv`. A\n  `done`-WI id lingering in `status.md` (e.g. a just-integrated predecessor)\n  trips `test_forward_only_unit_over_the_real_meta_repo` — that red is the\n  **integrator's** status regen to fix, not yours.\n\n- **`Verification=Critique` SRs (SR-052 dashboard a11y):** a render-surface\n  change re-fires the WI-243 perceptual-stale gate (WARN at commit bar, ERROR at\n  G3). Clearing needs a fresh **independent, family-heterogeneous** critique\n  (`docs/reviews/NNN-CRITIQUE.md` APPROVE vs `docs/rubrics/dashboard-\n  accessibility.md`) — the Claude builder can't self-certify it; flag it in the\n  commit, don't bury the warn. See [[ai-template-open-ideas]].\n","numLines":43,"startLine":1,"totalLines":43}}}
