this meta-repo's whole map** (its src is `project-trajectory/scripts`);\n    always pass the hook's args: `gen_arch_map.py --src project-trajectory/scripts\n    --doc docs/architecture.md`. The map's \"symbols\" mode tracks **internal\n    imports (incl. function-local ones) + public top-level symbols** — so a new\n    cross-module import or a new PUBLIC `def` stales it; an underscore-`_private`\n    def/helper does not.\n\n- **Avoid a new cross-component import (CMP-004↔CMP-001…):** the coordinator\n  (`agent_dispatch`/`agent_common`, CMP-004) importing a harness module\n  (`check`/`trace`/`check_trajectory`, CMP-001) adds an undeclared seam that\n  `check_trajectory --strict` turns to an **ERROR at G3** (WARN at the commit\n  floor). Precedent to follow (`agent_common` `OWNER_ONLY_PATHS` / WI-285\n  `_declared_test_command`): **mirror the small read into a same-component\n  (CMP-004) module** — `agent_common` — and pin it with a test, rather than\n  import across the boundary (which would owe an IF-### row + a `Contracts:`\n  docstring tag). Same-component edges (`agent_dispatch`→`agent_common`/\n  `agent_session`/`schedule`) are free.","originalFile":"---\nname: train-worktree-ops\ndescription: \"Operational facts for parallel-dispatch train worktrees (C:\\\\Projects\\\\ai-template-trains\\\\*) — which Python/venv to use and how a worker must handle generated artifacts vs the \\\"NEVER edit\\\" contract line.\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: c33a8229-9173-4168-8d0e-2fadb9f09bc3\n---\n\nWorking a parallel-dispatch WI in a train worktree under\n`C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\<train>\\` (branch `llm/train/...`):\n\n- **Toolchain venv:** these worktrees have **no local `.venv`**; ambient\n  `python` is old (3.8). Use the **main repo's** venv:\n  `C:\\Projects\\ai-template\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe` (Python **3.11.9**, has\n  pytest/xdist/ruff/pytest-cov). The pre-commit hook's own PY-probe finds no\n  worktree `.venv` and falls back to a PATH 3.12 that lacks ruff, so its\n  `format` step SKIPs — run `ruff format --check`/`check` yourself on the venv.\n\n- **Generated artifacts vs \"NEVER edit\":** the worker prompt says never edit\n  generated artifacts (dashboards, maps). That means don't *hand-edit/reconcile*\n  them — but the universal `.githooks/pre-commit` floor (`check.py --run-steps\n  arch-map,okf,trajectory-map,status-map,...`) **blocks a commit that leaves them\n  stale**. So when your source change stales one, **regenerate via the canonical\n  tool and commit it** (`gen_arch_map.py` for `docs/architecture.md`'s GENERATED\n  block; `gen_trajectory.py --root .` for `PROJECT_STATE.html`; regen order\n  arch-map→okf→dashboard). Precedent: worker commits `WI-219`/`WI-228` bundled a\n  regenerated dashboard. The integrator re-regenerates on the composed tree\n  (stack.ini `[generated]` auto-resolution, WI-235) — no re-review.\n\n- **Still off-limits on a train branch:** `docs/status.md`, `docs/run-state`,\n  `docs/log.md`, and the Status/Deliverable **cells** of `work-items.csv`. A\n  `done`-WI id lingering in `status.md` (e.g. a just-integrated predecessor)\n  trips `test_forward_only_unit_over_the_real_meta_repo` — that red is the\n  **integrator's** status regen to fix, not yours.\n\n- **`Verification=Critique` SRs (SR-052 dashboard a11y):** a render-surface\n  change re-fires the WI-243 perceptual-stale gate (WARN at commit bar, ERROR at\n  G3). Clearing needs a fresh **independent, family-heterogeneous** critique\n  (`docs/reviews/NNN-CRITIQUE.md` APPROVE vs `docs/rubrics/dashboard-\n  accessibility.md`) — the Claude builder can't self-certify it; flag it in the\n  commit, don't bury the warn. See [[ai-template-open-ideas]].\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":27,"oldLines":7,"newStart":27,"newLines":25,"lines":["   arch-map→okf→dashboard). Precedent: worker commits `WI-219`/`WI-228` bundled a","   regenerated dashboard. The integrator re-regenerates on the composed tree","   (stack.ini `[generated]` auto-resolution, WI-235) — no re-review.","+  - **arch-map footgun:** bare `gen_arch_map.py` defaults to `--src src` and","+    **WIPES this meta-repo's whole map** (its src is `project-trajectory/scripts`);","+    always pass the hook's args: `gen_arch_map.py --src project-trajectory/scripts","+    --doc docs/architecture.md`. The map's \"symbols\" mode tracks **internal","+    imports (incl. function-local ones) + public top-level symbols** — so a new","+    cross-module import or a new PUBLIC `def` stales it; an underscore-`_private`","+    def/helper does not."," ","+- **Avoid a new cross-component import (CMP-004↔CMP-001…):** the coordinator","+  (`agent_dispatch`/`agent_common`, CMP-004) importing a harness module","+  (`check`/`trace`/`check_trajectory`, CMP-001) adds an undeclared seam that","+  `check_trajectory --strict` turns to an **ERROR at G3** (WARN at the commit","+  floor). Precedent to follow (`agent_common` `OWNER_ONLY_PATHS` / WI-285","+  `_declared_test_command`): **mirror the small read into a same-component","+  (CMP-004) module** — `agent_common` — and pin it with a test, rather than","+  import across the boundary (which would owe an IF-### row + a `Contracts:`","+  docstring tag). Same-component edges (`agent_dispatch`→`agent_common`/","+  `agent_session`/`schedule`) are free.","+"," - **Still off-limits on a train branch:** `docs/status.md`, `docs/run-state`,","   `docs/log.md`, and the Status/Deliverable **cells** of `work-items.csv`. A","   `done`-WI id lingering in `status.md` (e.g. a just-integrated predecessor)"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
