{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdLUDJoZ12MiEvzaPB2oM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-285 is complete. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\n**The bug:** The serialized integrator's composed-tree bar (`agent_dispatch._run_combined_bar`) read the test command from `docs/stack.ini` `[stack] test`, but the kit declares its harness under `[product] test = {py} -m pytest` (the `check.py` schema). With no `[stack]` section, every integration journalled `\"skipped (no declared test command)\"` and treated the miss as a **pass** — so WI-275, WI-279, and all historical integrations landed without the composed-tree bar ever running. Integration-time gate verification was silently off.\n\n**The fix** (commit `db978f2`, 5 files, +242/−27):\n- New shared reader `agent_common._declared_test_command(ini)` resolves the declared command: kit schema `[product] test` with `{py}/{src}/{tests}` substitution (the same placeholders `check.py` fills), with legacy raw `[stack] test` as a fallback.\n- The skip is now **honest**: only a profile declaring *neither* key skips; a key present under a name the integrator didn't read no longer fail-opens, and a declared-but-empty command fails closed (never `subprocess([])`).\n\n**Key design decision:** The first cut imported `check` directly, but `check.py` is CMP-001 and `agent_dispatch` is CMP-004 — an undeclared cross-component import that `check_trajectory --strict` flags at G3. Since the resolver's *only* caller is the integrator, housing it in `check.py` wouldn't have shared one definition — just added a seam. So it lives in `agent_common` (the CMP-004 shared-primitives module the integrator already imports), mirroring `check.py`'s schema the way the existing `OWNER_ONLY_PATHS` mirrors `check_docs.SCRATCHPAD`, reusing `agent_session.split_cmd` (no new tokenizer). Dropping the now-dead `import shlex` shrank `agent_dispatch.py` by 1 line — module-size ratchet re-stamped downward (3533→3532), the sanctioned tightening.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Full unfiltered suite green: **1406 passed, 5 skipped**.\n- Pre-commit floor (arch-map / okf / trajectory / status-map / dashboard / privacy) all **PASS**; arch-map stayed fresh (no cross-component edge, private helper).\n- New tests: `[product]` causes the bar to RUN on a real integration (journals `result: pass`, not skipped); a red `[product]` bar parks; stackless-skip and legacy `[stack]` paths preserved; empty/unreadable profiles fail closed.\n- The only remaining cross-component warn is the pre-existing `gen_trajectory → schedule` one — I introduced none.\n\nThe spec (`docs/specs/WI-285.md`) records the Done-when checkoffs and the template/downstream disposition (the fix ships downstream verbatim; no schema change — `[product] test` was already the documented single home). Row-flip to `done` and spec archival are the integrator's close-ritual. Working tree is clean."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1647,"cache_read_input_tokens":272695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1647},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd0dd60f-8a41-4574-83c0-2662c4df9040","uuid":"50884685-e598-4b88-92ee-a3221fe0966c","request_id":"req_011CdLUDGgYwmfCrfV9HMyo3"}
